ence.","New pension annual monetary charge: £490 implied (£427 + £63 from switch charges assessment table) vs £512.69 stated (annual recurring charges table for Aviva Platform Personal Pension).","Initial advice fee: £4,794 (Our charges section) vs £4,794.37 (cashflow modelling inputs section) — £0.37 rounding difference.","Existing pension risk level: stated as 6 throughout (existing arrangements table and main recommendations) but alternative solutions section states one fund is risk profile 5 and the other risk profile 7."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["The fund value base used for the £512.69 new pension charge calculation (i.e. whether it includes the £3,600 new contribution or reflects a post-transfer value of ~£82,692) is not explicitly stated in the report, making it unclear whether the £490 and £512.69 are genuinely contradictory or computed on different bases."],"analysis":"Four internal inconsistencies are identified within the report itself.\n\n1. EXPENDITURE MISMATCH (High): The report states monthly expenditure as £2,493 in the 'Your current situation' narrative and £2,206 in the cashflow modelling inputs. The £287/month difference (approximately £3,444/year) is material and unexplained. No basis difference is offered — both purport to represent the client's current monthly outgoings. This affects whether the cashflow model accurately reflects the client's financial position and is a genuine internal contradiction on a figure that drives the recommendation analysis.\n\n2. NEW PENSION CHARGE MONETARY DISCREPANCY (High): The switch charges assessment table shows existing charge £427, impact £63, implying new plan = £490. The annual recurring charges table states the new Aviva Platform Personal Pension total charge as £512.69. The derived figures show that £427 at 0.54% and £63 at 0.08% are both computed on a base of approximately £79,074 (the existing fund value), while £512.69 at 0.62% implies a base of approximately £82,692 — which is £3,618 higher, consistent with the £3,600 new contribution being added. The report does not explain this basis difference. However, the 'Like for Like' comparison using £63 outperformance requirement is therefore applying the new plan's higher charge rate (0.62%) to the existing lower fund value (£79,074), which understates the new plan's actual cost (£512.69 vs £490). This is a material disclosure concern: the switch assessment underestimates the new plan's cost by £22.69/year because it does not account for the larger fund value the new plan will hold.\n\n3. INITIAL ADVICE FEE ROUNDING (Low): £4,794 vs £4,794.37 is a £0.37 rounding difference. This is trivial and falls within normal rounding tolerance.\n\n4. RISK LEVEL PRESENTATION (Moderate, but outside scope of this check): The risk level discrepancy (6 overall vs 5 and 7 for individual funds) relates to investment suitability and risk profiling, which falls under CHK-003/CHK-009 and should not be assessed here.\n\nThe two substantive findings for this check are: (a) the unexplained £287/month expenditure discrepancy between narrative and cashflow model, which is material to the financial planning basis; and (b) the £22.69 monetary charge discrepancy arising from different fund value bases being used in the switch assessment versus the charges table, which affects the accuracy of the switch cost disclosure. The rounding difference on the advice fee is noted but is not material.","citations":[{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — extractionReport/internalInconsistencies[0]","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Monthly expenditure","£2,493 per month (Your current situation section)","£2,206 per month (Cashflow modelling inputs section)","Difference: £287/month"]},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — extractionReport/internalInconsistencies[2]","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["New pension annual charge","£490 implied (£427+£63, switch charges assessment)","£512.69 stated (annual recurring charges table)","Difference: £22.69"]},{"passageId":null,"source":"Derived figures — Charge arithmetic","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Solution total ongoing","£512.69","0.62%","implied fund value £82,691.94"]},{"passageId":null,"source":"Derived figures — Charge arithmetic","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["EA1 impact","£63.00","0.08%","implied fund value £78,750.00"]},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model — extractionReport/internalInconsistencies[3]","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Initial advice fee","£4,794 (Our charges section)","£4,794.37 (Cashflow modelling inputs)","Difference: £0.37"]}],"issueCategories":["Data inconsistency"],"severity":"High","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

