rmation of the target income being met.","discrepancies":["The adviser notes [P3] record 'Defo 60?' suggesting uncertainty about whether the retirement age of 60 is fully confirmed by the client, while the report treats age 60 as a settled assumption throughout.","The DB pension income modelled in the report is stated as £22,000 gross per annum; this figure is not directly corroborated in the fact-find which records only £1,833/month gross (= £21,996/year, effectively consistent but not exactly £22,000 — immaterial rounding difference).","The cashflow modelling inputs use £2,206/month as current expenditure, while the 'Your current situation' section of the report states £2,493/month essential plus £800 discretionary — a material difference flagged as an internal inconsistency in the extraction; both figures appear in the report and neither is resolved as the operative figure for suitability purposes.","The target income of £2,200 net per month includes the DB pension, but the cashflow output documents in the file (P19, P21, P22) do not contain a tabular or explicit confirmation that the recommended strategy delivers this combined income at age 60 — the cashflow modelling section confirms the inputs but the output adequacy is not verified in the evidence.","The adviser notes [P3] flag uncertainty about when the client will stop part-time work ('When will he stop?'), which could affect the income bridge needed before full retirement at 60, but the report does not address this foreseeable income change."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":[],"analysis":"The core target income figure of £2,200 net per month is well evidenced in the fact-find [P1][P5] and is consistently stated in the report. The retirement age of 60 is recorded in the fact-find [P1] and used throughout the pension switch projections [P9][P13][P14]. The DB pension income of £1,700 net/month (£1,833 gross/month) from the fact-find [P15] is consistent with the £22,000 gross p.a. figure the report