e internal monetary inconsistency is a separate finding. Taken together, the gaps are moderate in severity: disadvantages are partially disclosed but material items (loss scenarios, drawdown depletion, death benefit tax, quantified tax exposure) are absent or delegated.","citations":[{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model /riskWarningsAndDisadvantages/limitations[]","category":"I","quote":"All other risks associated with this investment are detailed in the product literature provided to you. You should read this document carefully.","cells":null},{"passageId":null,"source":"Canonical model /recommendations[]/disadvantages[]","category":"I","quote":"including our 1% annual fee, the total cost is approximately 1.62% annually compared to your current arrangement of 0.54%. This means that your proposed plan will need to outperform your current plan by approximately 1.08% annually to match the same net growth.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P4","source":"Aviva - Pension - Key Features.md","category":"H","quote":"Your investments need to grow to compensate for the income you withdraw. If that doesn't happen, the income you take will deplete your pension fund. Especially if you choose to take a high level of income.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Aviva - Pension - Key Features.md","category":"H","quote":"If you die after the age of 75 we can pay the full value of your remaining pension fund to your nominated beneficiaries, at the discretion of the trustees. Any benefits will be taxed at your beneficiaries' marginal rate.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P3","source":"Aviva - Pension - Key Features.md","category":"H","quote":"The current favourable tax treatment of the Pension Portfolio may change if tax rules change.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P6","source":"Aviva Insured Funds Multi-Asset Plus II S14 - Factsheet.md","category":"H","quote":"B - Foreign Exchange Risk: When a fund invests substantially in overseas assets, its value will go up and down in line wi